  "identifier": "cdisc-sdtm",
  "name": "CDISC SDTM",
  "alternateName": [
    "Study Data Tabulation Model",
    "SDTM",
    "CDISC SDTM v3.4"
  ],
  "description": "The regulatory standard for organising and formatting clinical trial data submitted to the FDA and EMA. SDTM defines a set of domain models — subject demographics (DM), adverse events (AE), laboratory results (LB), vital signs (VS), medical history (MH), and ~40 other domains — each with standardised variable names, controlled terminology, and metadata. Required for all new drug and biologic NDA/BLA submissions to the FDA since 2016 and for EMA submissions via CDISC Harmonised Protocol. SDTM Implementation Guides (SDTMIGs) extend the base model for therapeutic area-specific data (oncology, cardiovascular, neuroscience). Maintained by CDISC (Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium), a non-profit standards body with pharmaceutical industry membership. Current version: SDTM v3.4 / SDTMIG v3.4 (2024). Open-source validation tooling available via the CDISC Rules Engine (github.com/cdisc-org/cdisc-rules-engine, MIT).",
  "url": "https://www.cdisc.org/standards/foundational/sdtm",
  "relatedLink": [
    "https://github.com/cdisc-org/cdisc-rules-engine",
    "https://www.cdisc.org/standards/therapeutic-areas"
  ],
